"\nTARGET 1 AGENTS.md prose\u002dentrypoint\nIDENTITY d41c545600fcd3f38584e585f25a2b75d688d0c3 c9cd148fbf052228d237a02e751e65b4d4edc2f39c75712b126650bc18715489 RANGES [[1, 356]] MASKED [48, 209]\n1: # AGENTS.md\n2: \n3: pixelelated is an **immutable Linux distribution for handheld gaming devices** (a ROCKNIX/JELOS fork\n4: built on the LibreELEC/CoreELEC cross\u002dcompilation system). There is no app to run \u2014 this\n5: repo is a *build system* that cross\u002dcompiles a complete OS image (kernel, bootloader,\n6: emulators, userland) per device.\n7: \n8: **Resuming work, or new to the project?** Read `.github/sessions/saved\u002dsession\u002dstate\u002dnext.md`\n9: on `next` first: the work in flight, what is running, the next commands, and a walk\u002dthrough\n10: for an agent who has never seen the project (D\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d133). A session loads the rules of the\n11: worktree it starts in, so check that yours carries `next`'s before trusting any of them:\n12: `git diff \u002d\u002dquiet next \u002d\u002d .claude CLAUDE.md AGENTS.md || echo STALE` \u002d\u002d then merge `next` into\n13: a feature worktree, or read the rules from `next` (#367).\n14: \n15: **How this file is read.** Codex reads `AGENTS.md` (this file, at the root; a nested\n16: `AGENTS.md` adds to its own subtree) and nothing else on its own, so this file stands\n17: alone: the commands, the rules that bind every session, and the list of every rule file\n18: with what it decides. Claude Code reads `CLAUDE.md` and loads `.claude/rules/*.md` by\n19: their `paths:` globs. Both files carry the same facts and are kept equal by\n20: `tools/rules\u002dcheck` (D\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d045), which also regenerates the rule list below from\n21: the rule files' own front matter. When something here and a rule file disagree, the rule\n22: file is right and this file has a bug.\n23: \n24: **Canonical deep\u002ddive docs (this file summarizes; they are authoritative):**\n25: \n26: \u002d `packages/README.md` \u2014 the authoritative `package.mk` format reference.\n27: \u002d `.claude/rules/*.md` \u2014 the canonical guides, all 30, listed below with their one\u002dline\n28:   descriptions and when each loads. `instruction\u002dfiles.md` is their index and carries the\n29:   front\u002dmatter standard (D\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d009). Open the every\u002dsession ones before starting;\n30:   open a scoped one before touching its paths.\n31: \u002d Two documents carry interface law and are loaded by no rule: `docs/es\u002dmenu\u002dmap.md`\n32:   (where a row belongs; D\u002dUI\u002d039: a row added, moved or renamed updates it in the same\n33:   change) and `docs/conflict\u002dwizard\u002dia.md` (the wizard's IA). `docs/device\u002dtesting\u002dpolicy.md`\n34:   is the device and QA\u002dguest policy.\n35: \n36: ## Current project identity\n37: \n38: The next RC is **pixelelated**, always lowercase (D\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d144).\n39: GitHub organization: `pixelelated`; maintainer: `rasteratops`; developer:\n40: `blitterbot`, unchanged. Rasteratops is a character, not the OS name.\n41: Use `/pixelelated` for new cloud setups (D\u002dCLOUD\u002d174/175).\n42: The required OS adoption path is ROCKNIX \u2192 pixelelated; no\n43: fielded Rasteratops migration gate exists. Preserve ROCKNIX stored interfaces,\n44: upstream credits and historical evidence. See `NAMING.md` and\n45: `docs/pixelelated/rename\u002dplan.md` before identity changes.\n46: \n47: Cloud setup uses normal linking and explicit folder selection (D\u002dCLOUD\u002d175).\n48: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n49: stay unchanged. Retire automatic cloud\u002dfolder migration and legacy joining or\n50: following under #508; users populate or rearrange their cloud folders themselves.\n51: OS upgrade preservation and normal sync/restore testing still apply.\n52: \n53: ## Build & development commands\n54: \n55: Builds are driven by `PROJECT` (default `ROCKNIX`), `DEVICE`, and `ARCH`. Per\u002ddevice make\n56: targets exist for: `RK3588`, `RK3576`, `RK3566`, `RK3326`, `RK3399`, `S922X`, `SM6115`,\n57: `SM8250`, `SM8550`, `SM8650`, `SM8750`, `H700`, `AMD64` (see `Makefile`; most build both\n58: `arm` and `aarch64`). `make world` builds the primary device set. The fork adds\n59: `GENERIC_X64`, the VM image every change is QA'd on first.\n60: \n61: Docker is the recommended way to build:\n62: \n63: ```bash\n64: make docker\u002dimage\u002dpull                   # pull Rasteratops mirror at Makefile's pinned digest\n65: make docker\u002dRK3588                       # full image build for a device\n66: make docker\u002dshell                        # interactive shell in the build container\n67: PACKAGE=retroarch make docker\u002dpackage    # build one package in the container\n68: ```\n69: \n70: Native equivalents (run from a path **without spaces**, **never as root**):\n71: \n72: ```bash\n73: make RK3588                              # device image build\n74: ./scripts/build <package>                # build ONE package\n75: ./scripts/clean <package>                # clean ONE package so it rebuilds\n76: make kconfig\u002dmenuconfig\u002dRK3588           # edit a device's kernel config\n77: scripts/checkdeps                        # verify host build dependencies\n78: ```\n79: \n80: Fast dev loop \u2014 rebuild one package, then remake the image instead of a full build:\n81: \n82: ```bash\n83: make docker\u002dshell                        # skip when building natively\n84: export PROJECT=ROCKNIX DEVICE=RK3588 ARCH=aarch64\n85: ./scripts/clean <pkg> && ./scripts/build <pkg>\n86: ./scripts/install <pkg> && ./scripts/image mkimage   # needs OS_VERSION/BUILD_DATE exported\n87: ```\n88: \n89: Native image/package entrypoints and Docker build targets automatically use\n90: `tools/watch\u002dbuild` and the shared `tools/watch\u002djob` monitor. Each run prints\n91: its private `.build\u002druns/<id>/` log, PID, result and status location; nested\n92: commands reuse it. Builds require a current single\u002duse capacity/retention admission\n93: from `tools/host\u002dmaintenance/build\u002dadmission` (#493); see its adjacent guide.\n94: Use `tools/watch\u002dbuild \u002d\u002dadmission RECEIPT \u002d\u002d COMMAND` for an ad\u002dhoc build.\n95: Non\u002dcompiling QA/record jobs use `\u002d\u002drecord\u002donly`; that mode cannot admit a nested build.\n96: Status recording does not send automatic chat notifications. See\n97: `device\u002dbuilds.md` for lifecycle and frozen\u002dcheckout handling.\n98: Long jobs also need verified result delivery; until off\u002dsession alerts are\n99: configured, supervise actively and announce completion promptly (#395).\n100: Result files belong to their producer: never pre\u002dfill a live owner's exit or\n101: completion receipts. Keep coordinator observations separate (#597).\n102: \n103: Images land in `target/` (`config/path` sets `TARGET_IMG=$ROOT/target`). Deploy to a\n104: networked device by `scp`\u002ding the image tar to `root@<host>:~/.update` and rebooting\n105: (preserves settings) \u2014 and both the copy and the reboot are the owner's yes, see below.\n106: \n107: **Testing/lint:** there is **no unit\u002dtest suite**. `tools/pkgcheck <package>` is the only\n108: package lint \u2014 run it after every `package.mk` edit. The real test is that the package or\n109: image builds, and then that `tools/vm\u002dqa` is green on the GENERIC_X64 image. A first build\n110: needs ~200GB disk and hours; cached rebuilds take minutes.\n111: \n112: ## Architecture\n113: \n114: **Layered config resolution** (`config/options`): options are sourced in order \u2014\n115: `distributions/<DISTRO>/options` \u2192 `projects/<PROJECT>/options` \u2192\n116: `projects/<PROJECT>/devices/<DEVICE>/options` \u2192 `config/arch.<ARCH>` \u2014 each layer\n117: overriding the last. Device knobs (CPU flags, kernel target, bootloader, GPU family) live\n118: in the device `options` file.\n119: \n120: **Package override model:** every package is a directory with a `package.mk`. A\n121: `package.mk` under `projects/<PROJECT>/packages/...` or\n122: `projects/<PROJECT>/devices/<DEVICE>/...` overrides the generic one of the same name in\n123: `packages/`. `DEVICE_ROOT` lets one device reuse another's build root.\n124: \n125: **Directory roles:**\n126: \n127: \u002d `packages/` \u2014 generic cross\u002dproject package recipes, grouped by function.\n128: \u002d `projects/<PROJECT>/` \u2014 SoC/vendor families (`ROCKNIX`, `Rockchip`, `Qualcomm`, ...):\n129:   device `options`, package overrides, `patches/`, `filesystem/` overlays, `bootloader/`.\n130: \u002d `distributions/ROCKNIX/` \u2014 distro identity (version, options, splash).\n131: \u002d `scripts/` \u2014 the build engine (`build_distro`, `build`, `clean`, `install`, `image`).\n132: \u002d `tools/` \u2014 dev helpers; most are upstream's, and the fork's own are enumerated by name\n133:   in `.claude/rules/fork\u002dworkflow.md` and `.githooks/pre\u002dpush`.\n134: \u002d `build.*/`, `sources/`, `release/`, `target/` \u2014 gitignored build outputs.\n135: \n136: **Emulator naming:** libretro cores are `*\u002dlr`; standalone emulators are `*\u002dsa`\n137: (`projects/ROCKNIX/packages/emulators/`).\n138: \n139: **EmulationStation** source lives in a separate git repo; see\n140: `projects/ROCKNIX/packages/ui/emulationstation/package.mk` for the pin and the extra build\n141: steps. An ES `.cpp` edit runs `tools/es\u002dsyntax\u002dcheck` before the pin moves.\n142: \n143: ## `package.mk` rules (see `packages/README.md` for the full reference)\n144: \n145: \u002d **Late\u002dbinding (enforced by `pkgcheck`):** toolchain/path vars (`CC`, `CFLAGS`,\n146:   `PKG_BUILD`, `TARGET_*`, ...) exist only *after* the package loads \u2014 reference them\n147:   **only inside functions** (`configure_package`, `pre_configure_target`, ...), never at\n148:   global scope.\n149: \u002d Customize via `pre_*`/`post_*` hook functions rather than replacing core build steps;\n150:   branch per device with `case ${DEVICE} in ... esac`.\n151: \u002d Preserve upstream JELOS/LibreELEC copyright headers and add a ROCKNIX line \u2014 this is a\n152:   fork; credits must be retained.\n153: \u002d Pin git sources with the **full** commit hash in `PKG_VERSION`.\n154: \u002d Patches in a package's `patches/` dir auto\u002dapply after unpack, and so do\n155:   `patches/<arch>/` (`x86` for an `x86_64` target, `scripts/unpack:127\u002d133`) and\n156:   `projects/<PROJECT>/devices/<DEVICE>/patches/<pkg>/` (`:159`); a per\u002ddevice\n157:   `patches/<DEVICE>/` inside the package applies only when the recipe adds it to\n158:   `PKG_PATCH_DIRS` (`:137\u002d145`). Kernel patches live under\n159:   `packages/linux/patches/<DEVICE>/`; hardware quirks under\n160:   `projects/ROCKNIX/packages/hardware/quirks/`. (T37 L\u002d18.)\n161: \n162: ## Commit conventions\n163: \n164: No Conventional Commits. Scope by package or device, matching history:\n165: `azahar\u002dsa \u002d bump to ...`, `SM8250 \u002d linux \u002d enable ntsync`, `emulationstation: bump package`.\n166: **Upstream PR commits are stricter** (CI\u002denforced): `package: text` title matching\n167: `^[a\u002dzA\u002dZ0\u002d9_*./\u002d]+:[[:space:]].+$`, \u226472 chars, blank line before body, no merge commits.\n168: \n169: ## Fork workflow (this working copy is a fork)\n170: \n171: `origin` = `pixelelated/distribution`, `upstream` = `ROCKNIX/distribution`. Full rules in\n172: `fork\u002dworkflow.md` / `worktrees.md`; the essentials:\n173: \n174: \u002d Branch `next` = `upstream/next` + a *personal overlay* (`.claude/`, `AGENTS.md`,\n175:   `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/`, `plans/`, `.githooks/`, the fork\u002donly tools). **Never PR `next`\n176:   upstream.**\n177: \u002d Feature work: branch `feature/<name>` from `next` in a worktree at\n178:   `../rocknix.worktrees/<name>`; the primary checkout stays on `next`. Build worktrees are\n179:   on `build/*` branches, never detached (D\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d004).\n180: \u002d Upstream PRs use a throwaway branch built **by content**: check out a detached\n"
